From 7473b7cec8a15afffc6f9b96191615ad190d83a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:46:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): edit each milling tool kind by its parameters
 inside the outline editor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Draw cutter view now carries the numbers each milling kind's outline
is drawn from (cutter Ø, the kind's tip - ball R, corner R, point or cone
angle - flute length, shank Ø and length) plus a neck, editing the same
draft as the editor's fields. A Parametric outline is redrawn from them;
a Custom one is carried onto the new numbers (cutter_fit::refit: tip
regenerated from the kind, the drawing above the flutes kept and moved,
clamped to the shank), so outline and numbers keep agreeing.

ReshapeTool lands the numbers and the drawn cutter together, one undo
step, judged against the new numbers; Apply cutter and the editor's
Apply use it instead of refusing a number edit under a drawn cutter.
MCP: set_tool_cutter_params; get_tool_cutter_profile reports the neck.

Refs #93

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
